## Hints

- E1: `idx = rng.integers(0, n, size=(B, n))`; then
  `x[idx]` is a (B, n) array of resamples — stat along axis=1.
  For block boot, each resample = concatenated blocks of length b,
  trimmed back to n.
- E3: the SE should roughly approach the naive SE × √(n/n_eff) —
  compare with the n_eff you can compute from the |r| ACF (04.1 E3).
